---
export const prerender = true;
import MarketingLayout from "../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro";
---

<MarketingLayout
  title="Limitations | CrawlPact"
  description="What CrawlPact cannot guarantee: declared policy is not proof of crawler behaviour, and other explicit product boundaries."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-reading px-4 py-12 sm:px-6">
    <h1 class="text-h1 text-neutral-950">Limitations</h1>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-h2 text-neutral-950">CrawlPact audits declared policy</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-body text-neutral-700">
      CrawlPact reports what a website's public configuration asks crawlers to do (declared policy)
      and what CrawlPact itself was able to retrieve (observed response). It does not, and cannot,
      prove what an external crawler actually does (actual crawler behaviour) —
      <code>robots.txt</code> and related signals are voluntary, unenforced declarations.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-h2 text-neutral-950">CrawlPact is not</h2>
    <ul class="mt-3 list-disc pl-5 text-body text-neutral-700">
      <li>A web application firewall or reverse proxy</li>
      <li>A live crawler blocker</li>
      <li>A server-log analytics service</li>
      <li>A full-site SEO crawler or general-purpose SEO suite</li>
      <li>An AI-search ranking tracker or brand-mention tracker</li>
      <li>A legal service or compliance certificate</li>
      <li>
        A guarantee that bots will obey instructions or that content will appear in AI answers
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-h2 text-neutral-950">Evidence can be incomplete</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-body text-neutral-700">
      A target may block CrawlPact's scanner, return an unexpected response, or expose only partial
      signals. When evidence is insufficient, CrawlPact shows "Incomplete" rather than a misleading
      score or result.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-h2 text-neutral-950">Registry coverage is not exhaustive</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-body text-neutral-700">
      CrawlPact's crawler registry only includes crawlers with a reliable official source and a
      verified token. An unlisted or newly introduced crawler will not appear in a report until it
      is verified and published.
    </p>
  </article>
</MarketingLayout>
